Z||000000||Mona||09-23-1999||12:40 AM||||Hi everybody! <BR>I was surfing the web & came across the web site for the Pontiac Historic Services.  <A HREF="http://www.phs-online.com" TARGET=_blank>www.phs-online.com</A> <BR>For $35.00 (US) and your VIN# they send you a VIN & Information Packet with a copy of the original factory invoice for your car ( I found out my Formula was delivered to a Pontiac dealer in Henderson, KY. ( I live in IN 2 1/2 hours north of Henderson) <BR>a copy of the dealer order form for that year, & other info. , In all I got 70 pages of stuff!<BR>I think it took 2 weeks to get it in the mail.<BR>Well, Just wanted to pass that along!<BR>-mona||||reg||14
Z||000001||DJRice||09-23-1999||08:32 AM||||Cool.  I had spotted that website as well and posted a note about it but apparently no one had used it and no one paid any attention to the post.  It sounds like it could be an interesting investment of $35.<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GT||09-23-1999||11:01 PM||||I already got my packet from the PHS on my Fiero.  I got a pic of a 87GT without the spoiler(looks odd).  I also got a bunch of info on colors and production numbers.  Some of the stuff got was pretty technical looking stuff.||||reg||10
Z||000003||Mona||09-24-1999||12:15 AM||||I had read in a corvette magazine, that if you write to your states' Bureau of Motor Vehicles, a person could find out the previous owners of your car,like I think as far back they will go back in Indiana was 10 years,.<BR>But, after sending the info about my car & a check for $8.00 , I got my check back and a form to fill out, stating why I wanted the information.  Sent it back ,I have yet to see anything,& it's been about 6 or 8 weeks.<BR>Has anybody ever found out the previous owners of their car?, You know, not the person you bought your car from but maybe the original owner.<BR>I just think it would be interesting info.<BR>Thanks!<BR>mona<BR>||||reg||1
